lse,\"signal\":\"SIGTERM\",\"timeout\":true},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\\n\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Command timed out after 120 seconds. If it needs longer and isn't waiting for input, rerun with a larger timeout.\\nExit code: 143 (SIGTERM)\"}],\"providerCall\":{\"executed\":false},\"providerResult\":{\"executed\":false},\"rawInput\":\"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"find /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public -maxdepth 2 -type d -name '*352*' 2>/dev/null; find /Users/michelkerkmeester -name 'measure-embedder-cost.mjs' -not -path '*/node_modules/*' 2>/dev/null | head -10\\\",\\\"workdir\\\":\\\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\\\"}\"},\"time\":{\"start\":1794522609447,\"end\":1794522730366}}}}\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/tasks.md:\n  Line 28: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `DOC` is `.skilled/commands/doctor`. `S` is this packet's `scratch/` folder. `X` is `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`. `E` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`. `C` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `M` is `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .attachedMetrics.plain, .metrics.false_offer'`. `P` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`. `R` is the phase 002 rollup query over `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`, as `../002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/tasks.md` T026 writes it. `D` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`.\n\n  Line 64: - [ ] T011 Add the embedding section to `E`: 30 query embeddings through the shared `OllamaAdapter` from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/dist/embeddings/adapters/ollama.js` with the `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` manifest from `registry.js`, printed as `warm.medianMs` and `warm.p95Ms`. When `/api/ps` listed no model before the first call, record that first call as `cold.firstCallMs` and the `ollama serve` resident memory as `idle.serveRssKb`. Otherwise print `cold: null` with the reason `model already loaded` (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c '.warm, .cold'` prints `n` 30, a median, a p95 and either `null` or a number.\n\n  Line 83: - [ ] T030 Add one entry for `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`: what it reads, that it writes and unloads nothing, its exit 2 and how to take a cold sample (`$ADV/scripts/README.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"measure-embedder-cost\" $ADV/scripts/README.md` prints at least one line.\n\n  Line 85: - [ ] T032 Run `E` with the model loaded (`$S/cost-warm.json`). Verify: `node $E > $S/cost-warm.json` exits 0 and `jq -c '[.model.sizeBytes, .memory.serveRssKb, .memory.runnerRssKb, .warm.medianMs, .warm.p95Ms, .cli.medianMs]' $S/cost-warm.json` prints six numbers.\n\n  Line 86: - [ ] T033 Run `E` again after the model unloaded on its own (`$S/cost-cold.json`). Wait until `curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq '.models | length'` prints 0, without unloading it by hand. Verify: `jq -c '[.cold.firstCallMs, .idle.serveRssKb]' $S/cost-cold.json` prints two numbers.\n\n  Line 87: - [ ] T034 Add row 5 `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` to the Step 2 table and renumber `/doctor:setup` to 6. Add a subsection \"Meaning Matching for Commands\" to section 2 with what a user gains, the cost table from T032 and T033 with the date (disk, idle memory, loaded memory, the 5 minute unload, warm and cold latency), the fact that the step asks before it pulls the model or starts the server and never installs Ollama, and the fact that a no keeps a phrase-only install. Add a troubleshooting row for `semantic_lane_off` (`INSTALL-SKILLED.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"meaning matching|skill-advisor embedder|semantic_lane_off\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md` prints at least three lines and each number in the table appears in `$S/cost-warm.json` or `$S/cost-cold.json`.\n\n  Line 114: - [ ] `$S/cost-warm.json` and `$S/cost-cold.json` hold the numbers the install guides print, and the degrade test reports 7 passed\n\n  Line 207: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Every cost number in `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` and `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` appears in `$S/cost-warm.json` or `$S/cost-cold.json`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/acceptance-criteria.md:\n  Line 52: `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `DOC` is `.skilled/commands/doctor`. `X` is `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`. `E` is `ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`. `C` is `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `M` is `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .attachedMetrics.plain, .metrics.false_offer'`. `R` is the phase 002 rollup query from `../002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/tasks.md` T026.\n\n  Line 56: | AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given Ollama running, When `E` runs once with the model loaded and once after it unloaded on its own, Then it prints the version, model size, serve and runner memory, loaded size and expiry, warm median and p95 over 30 calls, the CLI median over 5 calls and a cold first call and writes nothing. With the server unreachable it exits 2 naming the server | `node $E > scratch/cost-warm.json`, `node $E > scratch/cost-cold.json`, `OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9 node $E; echo $?` prints 2, and `git status --short` unchanged after each run | Unmet | - |\n\n  Line 61: | AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given `/doctor:install` and the install guides, When a user runs or reads them, Then the checklist prints the embedder route as step 5 before `/doctor:setup` as step 6, and both guides say the install sets up meaning matching by default behind a yes, give the measured cost with its date and say a no keeps a phrase-only install | `node DOC/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` exits 0, `rg -n \"meaning matching\\|skill-advisor embedder\\|semantic_lane_off\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `rg -n \"skill-advisor embedder\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` and each cost number found in `scratch/cost-warm.json` or `scratch/cost-cold.json` | Unmet | - |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"pattern\":\"cost-warm|measure-embedder|serveRssKb|firstCallMs\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\",\"include\":\"!**/node_modules/**\",\"limit\":50}"},"time":{"start":1794522751055,"end":1794522756144}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794522757926,"sessionID":"ses_e2e209366ffe3qZDn1hMKZPNUG","part":{"id":"prt_1d1e43b260010N2jNcwJY2UND7","sessionID":"ses_e2e209366ffe3qZDn1hMKZPNUG","messageID":"msg_1d1e407ea001ed1bUSHOUtqmJW","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"795cca4597a3e4d133cf060a01dc16d7a95e5a07","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1529,"output":232,"reasoning":306,"cache":{"read":78848,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794522762460,"sessionID":"ses_e2e209366ffe3qZDn1hMKZPNUG","part":{"id":"prt_1d1e44cdc001ogY862L7X0LmKg","sessionID":"ses_e2e209366ffe3qZDn1hMKZPNUG","messageID":"msg_1d1e43b2e001U3HLUQwJ8ARCOV","type":"step-start","snapshot":"56e782e89e00cb356a8d735e64a5bda78a6e0427"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794522821913,"sessionID":"ses_e2e209366ffe3qZDn1hMKZPNUG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1e5323d001r5mH9wEN1WUBWQ","sessionID":"ses_e2e209366ffe3qZDn1hMKZPNUG","messageID":"msg_1d1e43b2e001U3HLUQwJ8ARCOV","type":"tool","id":"call_ee995aaea91e4457bf6b58c1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md","offset":150,"limit":85},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md, lines 150-234\n150: | Root `README.md` (`:681`) | Yes, \"When the local embedder runs, a command row can also pass on meaning\" | No | No |\n151: | Advisor `README.md` (`:176`) | Yes, \"Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists\" | No | No |\n152: | Advisor `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` | Yes, section 12 explains the cascade and the registry. Section 2 lists no embedder and section 3 ends \"That is the whole install\" (`:72`) | No | No setup steps. `system-spec-kit/README.md:63` is the only file that says `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` |\n153: \n154: What the advisor does today, read from the code by symbol:\n155: - **Server absent.** `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding` (`ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts:110`) catches the error, sets `disabledReason` to `prompt_embedding_failed` only when no reason is set yet, prints `console.warn` to the daemon's stderr (`:160`) and scores with no prompt vector, so every command passes on its phrases alone. `outputWarnings` (`ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:509`) adds a warning only for a stale graph or a lane in `degradedLanes`, and `runtimeLaneHealthForStatus` (`:115`) marks only `graph_causal`, so the output carries no warning. The CLI run above shows `\"warnings\":null`.\n156: - **Model not pulled.** The adapter throws `OllamaModelNotLoadedError` and the advisor takes the same path as an absent server, with the same reason.\n157: - **Model cold.** Nothing preloads the model. The first prompt after 5 idle minutes pays the load inside the 5,000 ms query deadline.\n158: - **Slow call.** The query deadline is `OLLAMA_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS = 5_000` (`system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/adapters/ollama.ts:110`), overridden only by `OLLAMA_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS` (`:124`). The Claude hook passes a budget of `DEFAULT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS = 2500` (`hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:143`) and `.claude/settings.json:150` gives the hook 3 seconds. When the CLI child runs past its budget, `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli` returns its fail-open result with reason `timeout` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:559`). So a server that accepts the connection and never answers costs the whole brief, not only meaning matching. This is read from the code and not reproduced, because reproducing it needs a hung server.\n159: - **Status.** `readSemanticLaneHealth` (`ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts:157`) reads the active pointer, the `vec_<dim>` count and the last runtime reason. It never calls the server, so a server that went away since the last prompt still reads `laneEnabled: true`.\n160: \n161: Whether anything starts the server or pulls the model today: nothing does. `rg -n -i \"ollama serve|ollama pull|/api/pull|brew install ollama\"` over `.skilled` finds only documentation lines and the process sweeper's rule that preserves a running `ollama serve` (`.skilled/scripts/orphan-mcp-sweeper.sh:476`). The daemon picks the embedder once at start through `ensureActiveEmbedder` (`ADV/advisor-server.ts:380`), and when every probe fails it only logs a warning (`:387`). The startup scan indexes metadata only (`advisor-server.ts:154`), and `refreshSkillEmbeddings` is called from `skill_graph_scan` alone (`ADV/handlers/skill-graph/scan.ts:54`). A fresh clone or a copied project therefore has no vectors until someone runs that scan.\n162: <!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n163: \n164: ---\n165: \n166: <!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n167: ## 3. SCOPE\n168: \n169: ### In Scope\n170: - Commit `ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`, which records the model size, the resident memory of the server and its model runner, the loaded size, the keep-alive expiry, warm and cold embedding latency and advisor CLI latency as one JSON object. Without it no number in an install document can be reproduced.\n171: - Add the embedder's reachability and the command vector count to `advisor_status --include-semantic-health`, and add an `embedder` leg to `/doctor:setup` that reads them. Without them nothing a user runs shows that meaning matching is off.\n172: - Add the route `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`. It probes, prints a plan with the cost of each step, waits for a yes, runs only the approved steps, runs `skill_graph_scan` and checks the result. Without it the setup has no guided path.\n173: - Make the route one of the normal `/doctor:install` steps, printed as step 5 before `/doctor:setup`, and write its cost into `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` and the advisor's `INSTALL-GUIDE.md`. The step still shows its cost and waits for a yes. A user who says no keeps a working install that matches commands on phrases only.\n174: - Bound the prompt embedding with its own deadline of 750 ms, give a missing model and a timeout their own `disabledReason`, add a `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` warning to a recommendation that ran without a prompt vector and test the absent, model-missing, cold and slow cases.\n175: \n176: ### Out of Scope\n177: - Installing Ollama, pulling a model or starting the server during the build. For a user the route may pull the model and start the server after a yes. It never installs Ollama and prints the install command instead.\n178: - Changing the embedder cascade, the active model, the meaning bar of 0.72 and 0.02 or the `semantic_shadow` weight of 0.05. Phase 004 and packet `../../001-semantic-lane-enablement` own them.\n179: - A line in the hook brief. The operator chose the doctor, status and JSON warning surfaces, and phase 005 owns the brief head.\n180: - `AGENTS.md`. Nothing in this phase needs Gate 2 wording, and its size budget is checked by `/doctor:agents-md check`.\n181: - Fixing `includeEmbeddingsHealth`, which probes the hf-local socket. The guide is corrected to say so, and the new fields live in `includeSemanticHealth`.\n182: - Setting Ollama's `keep_alive`. The 5 minute unload is what keeps memory at the idle figure.\n183: \n184: ### Relation to `001-semantic-lane-enablement`\n185: That packet is Draft and owns skill-level embedding: the lane weight, skill vector coverage and its population pass. This phase owns the command-level setup a user sees. Three planned items touch the same ground and are recorded here so neither packet repeats the other.\n186: - Its phase 001 plans \"A read-only report of lane state, coverage and `disabledReason` on the advisor status surface\". `readSemanticLaneHealth` already ships it. This phase adds `backend` and `commandVectorCoverage` to the same object.\n187: - Its phase 001 also plans \"Recording daemon latency and cost per recommendation\". The script here measures the embedder's memory and latency and can serve as that record.\n188: - Its phase 002 plans the failure policy when the backend is unreachable during a scan. This phase covers the prompt-time query embedding only and leaves the scan's outage streak alone.\n189: Its file paths still name `mcp-server/`, which is now `runtime/`.\n190: \n191: ### Files to Change\n192: \n193: `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `DOC` is `.skilled/commands/doctor`.\n194: \n195: | File Path | Change Type | Description |\n196: |-----------|-------------|-------------|\n197: | `ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` | Create | The read-only measurement script |\n198: | `ADV/scripts/README.md` | Modify | One entry for the script |\n199: | `ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts` | Modify | Prompt embedding deadline and distinct reasons |\n200: | `ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`, `ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` | Modify | `backend` and `commandVectorCoverage` in the semantic lane health |\n201: | `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` | Modify | The `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` warning |\n202: | `DOC/_routes.yaml`, `DOC/skill-advisor.md` | Modify | The `embedder` route and its router row |\n203: | `DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` | Create | The route workflow |\n204: | `DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt` | Modify | The route's plan, approval and result wording |\n205: | `DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`, `DOC/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt` | Modify | The `embedder` leg and the target list row |\n206: | `DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml`, `DOC/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` | Modify | The embedder step as step 5, before `/doctor:setup` as step 6 |\n207: | `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` and the files `derive-command-bridges.cjs` regenerates | Modify | Activate the route's bridge like its six siblings |\n208: | `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` | Modify | The dependency, its cost and its setup |\n209: | `ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` | Create | Absent, model-missing, cold, slow and warning cases |\n210: | `ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`, `DOC/scripts/tests/skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`, `DOC/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | Modify | Status fields, the route contract and the six install steps |\n211: <!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n212: \n213: ---\n214: \n215: <!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n216: ## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n217: REQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n218: \n219: ### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n220: \n221: | ID | Requirement |\n222: |----|-------------|\n223: | REQ-001 | `node ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` prints one JSON object with the Ollama version, the model's size on disk, the resident memory of `ollama serve` and of its model runner, the loaded size and expiry from `/api/ps`, the median and p95 of 30 warm query embeddings, the median of 5 advisor CLI calls with distinct prompts and a cold sample taken only when `/api/ps` lists no loaded model. It writes, starts and unloads nothing. It exits 2 with a message naming the server when the server does not answer. |\n224: | REQ-002 | `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true` returns `backend` with `state` one of `reachable`, `unreachable` or `model_missing`, probed with one bounded `/api/tags` call of at most 500 ms, and `commandVectorCoverage` with `embedded` read from `vec_cmd_<dim>` and `total` the count of command entries that carry `embeddingText`. `laneEnabled` is false when `backend.state` is not `reachable`. |\n225: | REQ-003 | `/doctor:setup` runs a sixth leg, `embedder`, that reads REQ-002. It passes when `laneEnabled` is true and `commandVectorCoverage.embedded` is above 0, and otherwise reports DEGRADED with the repair `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`, never FAIL. Planner's reading, not the operator's words: the operator chose \"Set up by default, behind a yes\" and not \"Required\", so an absent embedder degrades the install and does not fail it. The route stays read-only. |\n226: | REQ-004 | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` probes read-only, prints a plan whose every step names its cost from REQ-001 and its undo, stops at an approval prompt and runs only approved steps. After the yes it may run `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` and start `ollama serve`. It never installs Ollama and prints the install command for the user instead. With `--dry-run` it stops after the plan. After the steps it runs `skill_graph_scan --trusted` and shows REQ-002. |\n227: | REQ-005 | The prompt embedding gives up after `PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS`, set to 750 ms. For an absent server, a missing model and a call past the deadline the recommendation equals the recommendation with no embedder, no error reaches the caller and `disabledReason` reads `prompt_embedding_unreachable`, `prompt_embedding_model_missing` or `prompt_embedding_timeout`. A cold call that answers inside the deadline is scored with its cosine. One test covers each of the four cases. |\n228: | REQ-006 | The `/doctor:install` checklist prints `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` as step 5, one of its normal steps, before `/doctor:setup` as step 6. `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` and the advisor's `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` state that the install sets up meaning matching by default and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, what it costs with the REQ-001 numbers and the date they were taken and that a user who says no keeps a working install that matches commands on phrases only. |\n229: \n230: ### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n231: \n232: | ID | Requirement |\n233: |----|-------------|\n234: | REQ-007 | A recommendation scored without a prompt vector carries the warning `semantic_lane_off:<disabledReason>` in `warnings`. The hook brief is unchanged. |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 235]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md, lines 150-234\n150: | Root `README.md` (`:681`) | Yes, \"When the local embedder runs, a command row can also pass on meaning\" | No | No |\n151: | Advisor `README.md` (`:176`) | Yes, \"Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists\" | No | No |\n152: | Advisor `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` | Yes, section 12 explains the cascade and the registry. Section 2 lists no embedder and section 3 ends \"That is the whole install\" (`:72`) | No | No setup steps. `system-spec-kit/README.md:63` is the only file that says `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` |\n153: \n154: What the advisor does today, read from the code by symbol:\n155: - **Server absent.** `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding` (`ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts:110`) catches the error, sets `disabledReason` to `prompt_embedding_failed` only when no reason is set yet, prints `console.warn` to the daemon's stderr (`:160`) and scores with no prompt vector, so every command passes on its phrases alone. `outputWarnings` (`ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:509`) adds a warning only for a stale graph or a lane in `degradedLanes`, and `runtimeLaneHealthForStatus` (`:115`) marks only `graph_causal`, so the output carries no warning. The CLI run above shows `\"warnings\":null`.\n156: - **Model not pulled.** The adapter throws `OllamaModelNotLoadedError` and the advisor takes the same path as an absent server, with the same reason.\n157: - **Model cold.** Nothing preloads the model. The first prompt after 5 idle minutes pays the load inside the 5,000 ms query deadline.\n158: - **Slow call.** The query deadline is `OLLAMA_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS = 5_000` (`system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/adapters/ollama.ts:110`), overridden only by `OLLAMA_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS` (`:124`). The Claude hook passes a budget of `DEFAULT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS = 2500` (`hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:143`) and `.claude/settings.json:150` gives the hook 3 seconds. When the CLI child runs past its budget, `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli` returns its fail-open result with reason `timeout` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:559`). So a server that accepts the connection and never answers costs the whole brief, not only meaning matching. This is read from the code and not reproduced, because reproducing it needs a hung server.\n159: - **Status.** `readSemanticLaneHealth` (`ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts:157`) reads the active pointer, the `vec_<dim>` count and the last runtime reason. It never calls the server, so a server that went away since the last prompt still reads `laneEnabled: true`.\n160: \n161: Whether anything starts the server or pulls the model today: nothing does. `rg -n -i \"ollama serve|ollama pull|/api/pull|brew install ollama\"` over `.skilled` finds only documentation lines and the process sweeper's rule that preserves a running `ollama serve` (`.skilled/scripts/orphan-mcp-sweeper.sh:476`). The daemon picks the embedder once at start through `ensureActiveEmbedder` (`ADV/advisor-server.ts:380`), and when every probe fails it only logs a warning (`:387`). The startup scan indexes metadata only (`advisor-server.ts:154`), and `refreshSkillEmbeddings` is called from `skill_graph_scan` alone (`ADV/handlers/skill-graph/scan.ts:54`). A fresh clone or a copied project therefore has no vectors until someone runs that scan.\n162: <!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n163: \n164: ---\n165: \n166: <!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n167: ## 3. SCOPE\n168: \n169: ### In Scope\n170: - Commit `ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`, which records the model size, the resident memory of the server and its model runner, the loaded size, the keep-alive expiry, warm and cold embedding latency and advisor CLI latency as one JSON object. Without it no number in an install document can be reproduced.\n171: - Add the embedder's reachability and the command vector count to `advisor_status --include-semantic-health`, and add an `embedder` leg to `/doctor:setup` that reads them. Without them nothing a user runs shows that meaning matching is off.\n172: - Add the route `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`. It probes, prints a plan with the cost of each step, waits for a yes, runs only the approved steps, runs `skill_graph_scan` and checks the result. Without it the setup has no guided path.\n173: - Make the route one of the normal `/doctor:install` steps, printed as step 5 before `/doctor:setup`, and write its cost into `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` and the advisor's `INSTALL-GUIDE.md`. The step still shows its cost and waits for a yes. A user who says no keeps a working install that matches commands on phrases only.\n174: - Bound the prompt embedding with its own deadline of 750 ms, give a missing model and a timeout their own `disabledReason`, add a `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` warning to a recommendation that ran without a prompt vector and test the absent, model-missing, cold and slow cases.\n175: \n176: ### Out of Scope\n177: - Installing Ollama, pulling a model or starting the server during the build. For a user the route may pull the model and start the server after a yes. It never installs Ollama and prints the install command instead.\n178: - Changing the embedder cascade, the active model, the meaning bar of 0.72 and 0.02 or the `semantic_shadow` weight of 0.05. Phase 004 and packet `../../001-semantic-lane-enablement` own them.\n179: - A line in the hook brief. The operator chose the doctor, status and JSON warning surfaces, and phase 005 owns the brief head.\n180: - `AGENTS.md`. Nothing in this phase needs Gate 2 wording, and its size budget is checked by `/doctor:agents-md check`.\n181: - Fixing `includeEmbeddingsHealth`, which probes the hf-local socket. The guide is corrected to say so, and the new fields live in `includeSemanticHealth`.\n182: - Setting Ollama's `keep_alive`. The 5 minute unload is what keeps memory at the idle figure.\n183: \n184: ### Relation to `001-semantic-lane-enablement`\n185: That packet is Draft and owns skill-level embedding: the lane weight, skill vector coverage and its population pass. This phase owns the command-level setup a user sees. Three planned items touch the same ground and are recorded here so neither packet repeats the other.\n186: - Its phase 001 plans \"A read-only report of lane state, coverage and `disabledReason` on the advisor status surface\". `readSemanticLaneHealth` already ships it. This phase adds `backend` and `commandVectorCoverage` to the same object.\n187: - Its phase 001 also plans \"Recording daemon latency and cost per recommendation\". The script here measures the embedder's memory and latency and can serve as that record.\n188: - Its phase 002 plans the failure policy when the backend is unreachable during a scan. This phase covers the prompt-time query embedding only and leaves the scan's outage streak alone.\n189: Its file paths still name `mcp-server/`, which is now `runtime/`.\n190: \n191: ### Files to Change\n192: \n193: `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `DOC` is `.skilled/commands/doctor`.\n194: \n195: | File Path | Change Type | Description |\n196: |-----------|-------------|-------------|\n197: | `ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` | Create | The read-only measurement script |\n198: | `ADV/scripts/README.md` | Modify | One entry for the script |\n199: | `ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts` | Modify | Prompt embedding deadline and distinct reasons |\n200: | `ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`, `ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` | Modify | `backend` and `commandVectorCoverage` in the semantic lane health |\n201: | `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` | Modify | The `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` warning |\n202: | `DOC/_routes.yaml`, `DOC/skill-advisor.md` | Modify | The `embedder` route and its router row |\n203: | `DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` | Create | The route workflow |\n204: | `DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt` | Modify | The route's plan, approval and result wording |\n205: | `DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`, `DOC/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt` | Modify | The `embedder` leg and the target list row |\n206: | `DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml`, `DOC/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` | Modify | The embedder step as step 5, before `/doctor:setup` as step 6 |\n207: | `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` and the files `derive-command-bridges.cjs` regenerates | Modify | Activate the route's bridge like its six siblings |\n208: | `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` | Modify | The dependency, its cost and its setup |\n209: | `ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` | Create | Absent, model-missing, cold, slow and warning cases |\n210: | `ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`, `DOC/scripts/tests/skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`, `DOC/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | Modify | Status fields, the route contract and the six install steps |\n211: <!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n212: \n213: ---\n214: \n215: <!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n216: ## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n217: REQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n218: \n219: ### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n220: \n221: | ID | Requirement |\n222: |----|-------------|\n223: | REQ-001 | `node ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` prints one JSON object with the Ollama version, the model's size on disk, the resident memory of `ollama serve` and of its model runner, the loaded size and expiry from `/api/ps`, the median and p95 of 30 warm query embeddings, the median of 5 advisor CLI calls with distinct prompts and a cold sample taken only when `/api/ps` lists no loaded model. It writes, starts and unloads nothing. It exits 2 with a message naming the server when the server does not answer. |\n224: | REQ-002 | `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true` returns `backend` with `state` one of `reachable`, `unreachable` or `model_missing`, probed with one bounded `/api/tags` call of at most 500 ms, and `commandVectorCoverage` with `embedded` read from `vec_cmd_<dim>` and `total` the count of command entries that carry `embeddingText`. `laneEnabled` is false when `backend.state` is not `reachable`. |\n225: | REQ-003 | `/doctor:setup` runs a sixth leg, `embedder`, that reads REQ-002. It passes when `laneEnabled` is true and `commandVectorCoverage.embedded` is above 0, and otherwise reports DEGRADED with the repair `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`, never FAIL. Planner's reading, not the operator's words: the operator chose \"Set up by default, behind a yes\" and not \"Required\", so an absent embedder degrades the install and does not fail it. The route stays read-only. |\n226: | REQ-004 | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` probes read-only, prints a plan whose every step names its cost from REQ-001 and its undo, stops at an approval prompt and runs only approved steps. After the yes it may run `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` and start `ollama serve`. It never installs Ollama and prints the install command for the user instead. With `--dry-run` it stops after the plan. After the steps it runs `skill_graph_scan --trusted` and shows REQ-002. |\n227: | REQ-005 | The prompt embedding gives up after `PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS`, set to 750 ms. For an absent server, a missing model and a call past the deadline the recommendation equals the recommendation with no embedder, no error reaches the caller and `disabledReason` reads `prompt_embedding_unreachable`, `prompt_embedding_model_missing` or `prompt_embedding_timeout`. A cold call that answers inside the deadline is scored with its cosine. One test covers each of the four cases. |\n228: | REQ-006 | The `/doctor:install` checklist prints `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` as step 5, one of its normal steps, before `/doctor:setup` as step 6. `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` and the advisor's `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` state that the install sets up meaning matching by default and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, what it costs with the REQ-001 numbers and the date they were taken and that a user who says no keeps a working install that matches commands on phrases only. |\n229: \n230: ### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n231: \n232: | ID | Requirement |\n233: |----|-------------|\n234: | REQ-007 | A recommendation scored without a prompt vector carries the warning `semantic_lane_off:<disabledReason>` in `warnings`. The hook brief is unchanged. |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 235]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md\",\"offset\":150,\"limit\":85}"},"time":{"start":1794522821181,"end":1794522821913}}}}
